  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes rational design of quinoline analogues as noncovalent inhibitors of SARS-CoV-2 papain-like protease by targeting the Val70Ub pocket, with crystallographic confirmation of Val70Ub engagement by Jun13296 and reported antiviral-candidate properties motivating further development against coronaviruses.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A structure-guided antiviral discovery pattern: if a designed inhibitor series targets a specific protease pocket and a lead compound is structurally confirmed to engage that pocket, then the series and lead can motivate further optimization of protease inhibitors."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) This work designs quinoline analogues to target the Val70Ub site, and X-ray crystal structures confirm that Jun13296 is among the compounds whose 2-aryl substituent occupies the Val70Ub site."];
  "S28" [label="(28,0,0) In this work, we design a series of quinoline analogs to similarly target the Val70Ub site."];
  "S29" [label="(29,0,0) X-ray crystal structures confirm the 2-aryl substituent occupies the Val70Ub site as expected for five compounds including Jun13296."];
